  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asian Elephant Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to build on the background research and extensive experience that Elephant Family, the Wildlife Protection Society of India (WPSI) and the Wildlife Society of Odisha (WSO) have generated through working in partnership since 2005. Applicant will engage local communities in conservation by providing support, advice and information through regular meetings and one large workshop. Four local wildlife conservation groups will be empowered to raise awareness, attract new members and help the Forest Department intervene when illegal activity is posing a threat to elephants, while also alerting the project team to other threats to elephants in their area. Threats from industrial activity will result in dialogue with the company responsible. This approach has proved effective in the past and will be extended to tackle further threats, such as the deaths of elephants by electrocution from low-hanging power cables, which is an issue on which the three partner organizations have been working on for the past two years. HEC mitigation assistance will be provided to 30 villages. The project will also sustain an awareness program and forest protection committees at Simlipal National Park.</narrative>
  </description>
